WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.232
Here is the PostgreSQL-native approach to common
temporal tasks Subtract

00:00:06.258 --> 00:00:12.122
timestamps to obtain an interval Add INTERVAL values
to shift time

00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:19.687
Use EXTRACT to read components Use DATE_TRUNC to
change

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.451
analytical grain Use AGE when you want a symbolic
calendar

00:00:25.477 --> 00:00:31.135
interval These patterns are clearer and more
portable within PostgreSQL

00:00:31.162 --> 00:00:34.122
than borrowing function names from another SQL
dialect
